======================================================================================================================
A1  THE TASK'S CURRENT IN THE NR LIMIT: J.n is the clock-frame number density, J^i the (reversed) number flux
======================================================================================================================
  [PASS] A1 DERIVED: with Psi = e^{-imt} a e^{i theta}/sqrt(2m), J.n = a^2 (1 - theta_t/m) -> n_d (the number density in the clock frame) and J^x = -a^2 theta_x/m = -n_d v: a coupling to J.n is a density coupling, a coupling to the spatial J is a coupling to the dark flux
         measured: J^0 = (-m + Derivative(theta(t, x), t))*a(t, x)**2/m; J^x = -a(t, x)**2*Derivative(theta(t, x), x)/m; residuals 0, 0

======================================================================================================================
A2  GAUGE REDUCTION: a current coupling is a charged scalar in an external potential plus a DENSITY coupling
======================================================================================================================
    -|dPsi|^2 - m^2|Psi|^2 + g A.J  -  [ -|(d + i g A)Psi|^2 - m^2|Psi|^2 + g^2 A.A |Psi|^2 ] = 0
    A = d chi, Psi = e^(-i g chi) Psi':  L - [ -|dPsi'|^2 - m^2 |Psi'|^2 + g^2 (d chi)^2 |Psi'|^2 ] = 0
    so: (c) g J.d chi is FP4's density class at O(g^2) (m^2 -> m^2 - g^2 (d chi)^2: a WELL for spatial gradients);
        (b) g (J.n) f: A = f n, A.A = -f^2 -> an electrostatic potential g f per particle plus m^2 -> m^2 + g^2 f^2 (healthy);
        (e) spatial A: only B = curl A (magnetic, no work) and E = -d_t A are physical
  [PASS] A2 DERIVED (gauge reduction): -|dPsi|^2 + g A.J == -|(d + igA)Psi|^2 + g^2 A.A |Psi|^2 identically, and for A = d chi the field redefinition removes the current coupling exactly, leaving the density coupling g^2 (d chi)^2 |Psi|^2
         measured: identity residual 0; gradient-reduction residual 0
         reading:  a current coupling to a gradient does nothing at O(g) (pure gauge) and is FP4's density class at O(g^2); a coupling to J.n is an electrostatic potential, i.e. FP4's class; only a curl (magnetic) or a clock-frame rate survives

======================================================================================================================
A3  REST-ENERGY REDUCTION: the kinetic couplings' dispersion; which are density couplings, which change inertia
======================================================================================================================
    isotropic -F(I) g^mn        : rest energy m*sqrt(1/(F + 1)); 1/inertia (F + 1)*sqrt(1/(F + 1))/m (along e: (F + 1)*sqrt(1/(F + 1))/m); speed^2 1 (along e: 1)
    temporal -F(I) n^m n^n      : rest energy m*sqrt(1/(F + 1)); 1/inertia sqrt(1/(F + 1))/m (along e: sqrt(1/(F + 1))/m); speed^2 1/(F + 1) (along e: 1/(F + 1))
    spatial -G(I) h^mn          : rest energy m; 1/inertia (G + 1)/m (along e: (G + 1)/m); speed^2 G + 1 (along e: G + 1)
    anisotropic -G(I) e^m e^n   : rest energy m; 1/inertia 1/m (along e: (G + 1)/m); speed^2 1 (along e: G + 1)
    isotropic member: V/c^2 = sqrt(1/(F + 1)) - 1 per unit rest mass (a density coupling, luminal); a hill of v^2/2 needs F = -1 + 4/(beta + 2)**2; |F|/(FK1 eps/m^2) = 2 - 5*beta/2 + O(beta^2): 575.0 km/s 3.679e-06 (2.0000x), 600.0 km/s 4.006e-06 (2.0000x), 625.0 km/s 4.346e-06 (2.0000x), 650.0 km/s 4.701e-06 (2.0000x)
  [PASS] A3 DERIVED (rest-energy reduction): -F(I) g^{mn} dPsi* dPsi is exactly the density coupling V = c^2[(1+F)^(-1/2) - 1] (rest energy m/sqrt(1+F), luminal); the temporal member shifts the rest energy AND the speed (1/(1+F)); the spatial and anisotropic members leave the rest energy and change only the inertia; a 575-650 km/s hill needs |F| = 2.0 x FK1's eps/m^2
         measured: V_iso = sqrt(1/(F + 1)) - 1; |F|/(eps/m^2) = 2 - 5*beta/2; 575.0: 1.99999, 600.0: 1.99999, 625.0: 1.99999, 650.0: 1.99999
         reading:  the derivative door is the density door with a different name: the kinetic coupling's hill is a rest-mass hill, FK1's latent heat written as a place-dependent mass, and it pays FP4's reciprocity exactly

======================================================================================================================
A4  THE ENERGY-RECIPROCITY IDENTITY: energy reaches the dark state from the MOND sector only through S, its back-reaction
======================================================================================================================
    particle: h = m*Phi(x) - 3*v**4*W4(x, t) + v**2*(m/2 - W2(x, t)) + W0(x, t);  dh/dt - dW/dt|_(x,v) on shell = 0;  h contains W1: False
    field: -dL_int/dt|_dark + S u'_t + d/dt(Pi u'_t) = 0  (S = dL/du' - dPi/dt, Pi = dL/du'_t: generic L_int)
    bound: P u'_t - (a0^2 q'/8 pi G) dI/dt = 0  (P = q' u'/4 pi G; u'_t parallel to u')  =>  energy per volume between static
           epochs <= max(delta) (a0^2/8 pi G) q(I): the MOND sector can hand over at most max(delta) x its own field energy
  [PASS] A4 DERIVED (the energy-reciprocity identity): for a particle, dh/dt = dW/dt|_(x,v) and h has no linear-in-v part (a static current coupling does no work); for any L_int(grad u, d_t grad u, dark fields) the dark state's energy changes as -S.d_t grad u - d_t(Pi.d_t grad u) with S its source in the MOND sector's equation; with |S| <= delta |P| the energy handed over between static epochs is <= max(delta) x the MOND field energy (a0^2/8 pi G) Int q(I) for a field growing in magnitude
         measured: particle residual 0 (W1 in h: False); field residual 0; flux-energy residual 0
         reading:  no coupling -- density, current, derivative, rate, any order, any velocity weighting -- can take energy from the MOND sector without an equal source S in the MOND sector's own equation; couplings only choose WHEN they pay it

======================================================================================================================
A5  THE EXACT BACK-REACTION ON THE MOND SECTOR'S SOURCE, member by member (Euler-Lagrange of I_NR + L_int, spherical)
======================================================================================================================
    density  -rho_d V(I)                        : S = -2*rho_d(r, t)*Derivative(u(r, t), r)*Subs(Derivative(V(_xi_1), _xi_1), _xi_1, Derivative(u(r, t), r)**2/a_0**2)/a_0**2;  EL - d_r[r^2 flux] = 0
    rate     -g n_d d_t I  (== g J_perp.grad I) : S = 2*g*Derivative(n(r, t), t)*Derivative(u(r, t), r)/a_0**2;  EL - d_r[r^2 flux] = 0
    inertia  -G(I) rho_d w^2/2                  : S = -rho_d(r, t)*w(r, t)**2*Derivative(u(r, t), r)*Subs(Derivative(Gcoef(_xi_1), _xi_1), _xi_1, Derivative(u(r, t), r)**2/a_0**2)/a_0**2;  EL - d_r[r^2 flux] = 0
    current  g j F(I) u'  (J_perp . F grad u)   : S = g*(a_0**2*F(Derivative(u(r, t), r)**2/a_0**2) + 2*Derivative(u(r, t), r)**2*Subs(Derivative(F(I_s), I_s), I_s, Derivative(u(r, t), r)**2/a_0**2))*j(r, t)/a_0**2;  EL - d_r[r^2 flux] = 0
    Phi-equation: Lap u = 4 pi G rho (residual 0), unchanged by every member
    => with a regular centre Phi' = u' (1 + q') + 4 pi G S = u' [1 + q'(1 - delta)], delta = -4 pi G S/(q' u'):
       density: delta = 8 pi G rho_d V'/(a0^2 q')  (FP4 B1);  rate: delta = -8 pi G g d_t n_d/(a0^2 q')  (zero for a static dark state);
       inertia: delta = 8 pi G G' (rho_d w^2/2)/(a0^2 q');  current: S = g j (F + 2 I F'), proportional to the dark current
  [PASS] A5 DERIVED: the Euler-Lagrange equations of I_NR + L_int give Phi' = u'(1 + q') + 4 pi G S for every member (residual 0), with S = -2 rho_d V' u'/a0^2 (density), 2 g (d_t n_d) u'/a0^2 (rate: the n_d d_t u' terms cancel), -G' rho_d w^2 u'/a0^2 (inertia), g j (F + 2 I F') (current); the Poisson equation for u is untouched
         measured: residuals density 0, rate 0, inertia 0, current 0; Poisson 0
         reading:  the current and rate members write on the phantom only while the dark state FLOWS (j != 0, d_t n_d != 0): in a static halo they are silent -- and, by A4, they hand over nothing there either
  part A done   [23s]

